WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:18.267
Start from the SSC Vault diagram

2
00:00:18.267 --> 00:00:42.333
Open the Vault from the browser box

3
00:00:42.333 --> 00:01:01.400
Choose FastSolv and scroll to its input

4
00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:25.200
Submit one value and watch the job appear

5
00:01:25.200 --> 00:02:27.867
Return to the map: admission and dispatch

6
00:02:27.867 --> 00:03:25.133
Follow the map into GitHub Actions

7
00:03:25.133 --> 00:04:14.467
Open the runner source from the same box

8
00:04:14.467 --> 00:05:26.067
Follow the module package to its Python entrypoint

9
00:05:26.067 --> 00:06:16.600
Return to the map for the file-input path

10
00:06:16.600 --> 00:06:38.800
Submit the image through the same job interface

11
00:06:38.800 --> 00:07:31.600
The file is staged after admission

12
00:07:31.600 --> 00:08:35.800
The manifest selects the container and output

13
00:08:35.800 --> 00:09:29.200
Return through the callback box

14
00:09:29.200 --> 00:10:27.733
Follow the result into Supabase

15
00:10:27.733 --> 00:11:40.600
Open the private results bucket from the map

16
00:11:40.600 --> 00:12:41.200
Return to the map for result retrieval

17
00:12:41.200 --> 00:13:34.133
The browser follows the job lifecycle

18
00:13:34.133 --> 00:14:37.333
Return from the map to the completed value job

19
00:14:37.333 --> 00:15:09.933
Compare the completed image result

20
00:15:09.933 --> 00:16:08.867
Check the completed container workflow

21
00:16:08.867 --> 00:16:54.533
Read the complete request sequence

22
00:16:54.533 --> 00:17:12.933
Keep the organization and job records connected

23
00:17:12.933 --> 00:17:35.600
The same loop, at a simpler level
